# Lychee link-checker ignore file.
#
# Each non-comment line is a regex matched against the full URL
# (scheme + host + path + fragment). A URL is skipped if the regex
# matches it. Comments start with `#`.
#
# The validation workflow and `scripts/validate-local.sh` run lychee
# against `**/*.{md,ts,svelte}` with `--offline`. Use this file for
# URL / host patterns; pass file-system exclusions via
# `--exclude-path` in the workflow instead.

# Localhost / loopback hosts.
^https?://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|0\.0\.0\.0|\[?::1\]?)(:\d+)?(/|$|\?)

# Mailto links cannot be checked offline.
^mailto:
#
# NOTE on file:// URLs: lychee v0.24.x has a quirk where any
# .lycheeignore pattern containing the substring "file" causes
# every URL in the input to be excluded (the regex is treated as
# a glob for that scheme). So we deliberately do not exclude
# file:// here. The behaviour we want is: file:// links to files
# that do not exist on disk surface as ERROR in the lychee log
# but do NOT fail the job — lychee returns exit 0 for missing
# file targets. Parse failures (invalid URL syntax) DO fail with
# exit 2; those are real defects and should be fixed.
